@startuml spring_loaded_brake_fsm

legend top
1.  In order to provide a fail-safe braking mechanism, spring loaded brakes achieve full braking power, when they are "inactive".
    In order to release the spring loaded brakes of a tram, a spring is loaded by a pump - usually by applying a voltage to it.
    (Spring loaded brakes can also be released by pumping manually, but that is only done, when there are technical errors.)
    Thanks to that system a tram will always be able to brake, even if it loses all power (from the battery).
2.  Transitions are not labeled in detail, since the core logic will be modelled in a supervisor model
3.  Loss of power is a global physical transition from each state towards STATE_SLB_APPLIED. These transitions are omitted to keep this diagram readable.
endlegend

state SPRING_LOADED_BRAKE_FSM {
    state STATE_SLB_APPLIED
    state STATE_SLB_APPLYING
    state STATE_SLB_INTERMEDIATE
    state STATE_SLB_RELEASING
    state STATE_SLB_RELEASED


    STATE_SLB_APPLIED: output: slb_applied
    STATE_SLB_APPLIED: this state is also the fail-safe end state, if the vehicle loses all power from the battery (release force is lost)
    STATE_SLB_APPLIED: braking force = 100%

    STATE_SLB_APPLYING: output: slb_applying
    STATE_SLB_APPLYING: braking force increasing

    STATE_SLB_RELEASING: output: slb_releasing
    STATE_SLB_RELEASING: braking force decreasing

    STATE_SLB_RELEASED: output: slb_released
    STATE_SLB_RELEASED: braking force = 0%

    STATE_SLB_INTERMEDIATE: output: slb_intermediate
    STATE_SLB_INTERMEDIATE: 0% < braking force < 100%
    STATE_SLB_INTERMEDIATE: stable intermediate braking force


    [*] --> STATE_SLB_APPLIED: tram powered on
    STATE_SLB_APPLIED --> [*]: tram powered off

    STATE_SLB_APPLIED --> STATE_SLB_RELEASING
    STATE_SLB_RELEASING --> STATE_SLB_RELEASED : fully released

    STATE_SLB_RELEASED --> STATE_SLB_APPLYING
    STATE_SLB_APPLYING --> STATE_SLB_APPLIED : full application reached


    STATE_SLB_APPLYING --> STATE_SLB_RELEASING : applying slb is reversed
    STATE_SLB_RELEASING --> STATE_SLB_APPLYING : releasing slb is reversed

    STATE_SLB_INTERMEDIATE --> STATE_SLB_APPLYING : more braking power requested
    STATE_SLB_APPLYING --> STATE_SLB_INTERMEDIATE : intermediate target reached

    STATE_SLB_INTERMEDIATE --> STATE_SLB_RELEASING : less braking power requested
    STATE_SLB_RELEASING --> STATE_SLB_INTERMEDIATE : intermediate target reached
}

@enduml